      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2012, Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "The aim of the study was to investigate the relationship between severity of coronary artery disease (CAD) assessed with SYNTAX score (SS) and myocardial performance index (MPI) in stable CAD."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "The study participants consisted of 106 consecutive patients (mean age: 57.6 ± 9.5 years) with angiographically proven obstructive stable CAD and 30 patients with nonobstructive CAD (control group) (mean age: 58.0 ± 7.6 years). The MPI was calculated by using pulsed-wave Doppler before coronary angiography. Coronary angiography was performed in all patients. The SS was prospectively calculated in 106 obstructive CAD patients. Patients were partitioned into 3 groups based on SS. Frequencies of risk factors, biochemical and hematological data were recorded in all patients."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "The SS tertiles were defined as SS(low) ≤ 8 (n = 35), SS(mid) ≤ 17 (n = 36), and SS(high) > 17 (n = 35). The patients with SS(high) group (mean MPI; 0,48 ± 0.06) based on SS had significantly higher MPI values compared with the SS(mid) (mean MPI; 0,44 ± 0.05), SS(low) (mean MPI; 0.43 ± 0.06), and control (mean MPI; 0.41 ± 0.05) groups (P < 0.05 for all). The MPI levels of control group were also lower than compared with SS(mid) group (P = 0.006). The MPI value was significantly correlated with SS (r = 0.564, P < 0.001), diabetes (r = 0.355, P < 0.001), hypertension (r = 0.326, P < 0.001), and ejection fraction (EF) (r = -0.224, P = 0.018) in bivariate analysis. Multivariate regression analysis showed that MPI was independently associated with SS (β = 0.486, P < 0.001) and diabetes (β = 0.205, P = 0.028)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "Although the normal EF, MPI value was impaired in proportion to the severity of CAD in patients with stable CAD."
          }
        ]
      },
